**/.git
**/.vs
**/.idea
**/.claude
**/bin
**/obj
**/node_modules
login-app/dist
**/*.md
**/*.user
**/*.suo
# Recursive, matching the **/ rules above. Root-anchored patterns excluded only the top-level
# copies, so a nested demos/*/.env or src/*/appsettings.Production.json — exactly where real
# per-environment secrets live — was copied into the image and shipped.
**/.env*
**/appsettings.*.json
!**/appsettings.json
# appsettings.Development.json is NOT re-admitted. Nothing in any image needs it — no Dockerfile or
# compose file here sets ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Development — but shipping it means anyone who does
# set that variable on a deployed container silently repoints Issuer at https://localhost:5001 and
# Storage at the Azurite emulator, from a file they never wrote and cannot see in their own config.
